data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** Cas9 nuclease guided by a synthetic RNA cuts DNA at a chosen site [1]. These programmable \"molecular scissors\" create double-strand breaks that allow DNA to be inserted, deleted, modified, or replaced [3].\n- **Biological origin:** CRISPR-Cas9 is a simplified version of a bacterial antiviral defense system [1]. Bacteria and archaea store fragments of phage DNA to detect and destroy similar phages in later infections [2].\n- **Medical claims outpace evidence:** Headlines report disease applications, including a 2021 claim about treating a broad range of diseases [4] and a 2024 report that HIV was eliminated in cell culture [5]. The research provided doesn't establish clinical outcomes, so these should be treated as preliminary."}

